{
  "$comment": "Conformance vectors for carrier equivalence, normative in kernel/specs/controller-protocol.md §11. Every table here is normative. `payload` is one message body as a typed frame; `abi.buffer` is the bytes the ABI carrier's TeloBuf holds for it, and `framed.frame` is the whole framed-carrier frame carrying the same body. `abi.buffer` MUST be exactly the UTF-8 bytes of `payload`, and `framed.frame` MUST contain them unchanged — the framed carrier adding only its header and the envelope's other members. A chunk rides beside the payload on both carriers, so a Channel.Data row's `abi.chunk` and the frame's data region are the same bytes. Together the rows cover every section of the message set, which is what 'no message exists on one carrier only' asserts.",
